   "source": [
    "## 1.5 Stage-0 baseline modal split - Forch Mobility Hub\n",
    "\n",
    "Before testing interventions, this section reports the reference (Stage 0) mode choice for the configured Forch corridor. Public Transport combines walk-access and bicycle-access PT; the model internally retains both alternatives.\n",
    "\n",
    "The aggregate scope is every modeled OD pair with at least one endpoint in the corridor. The two named municipality groups in `parameters.py` define the Forch catchment comparisons; municipalities outside those groups appear as **Rest of Canton**. This is a municipality-level catchment analysis, not a station-level forecast.\n",
    "\n",
    "Trip shares use all peak-hour trips in scope. For this Mobility Hub, PKM includes every trip with a finite modeled route distance (0 km lower threshold): short access trips are important to the project, so the MehrSpur example's 5 km strategic filter is not appropriate. Any positive trips lacking a finite distance are excluded from PKM and explicitly reported. PKM uses each mode's own route-distance skim (both PT access alternatives are weighted separately), not car distance as a proxy."
   ]
  },
