   "source": [
    "The chart contains checked road-relative-gap values. Runs that stop earlier do not contribute to later-iteration summaries. A run that reaches the iteration cap before the target is reported as unconverged; increasing the cap is a separate modeling choice.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "coupled-msa-note",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Closing the loop: modal split inside the MSA iteration\n",
    "\n",
    "The fixed-demand dashboard above updates road routes and link travel times, but it assigns traffic based on an OD matrix that was estimated only once from uncongested travel time skims. Congestion is therefore not yet considered within the choice set of a traveller deciding between public transport, bicycle, walking, or a PT access alternative. The following workflow includes congestion effects in the consideration using the same MSA sequence:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. The BPR function is used to update every road-link travel time from the current traffic volume.\n",
    "2. The shortest paths algorithm produces the subsequent link traffic-volume target.\n",
    "3. Travel times between every internal zone and direction-compatible cordon gate are recorded at both free flow and current congestion levels.\n",
    "4. The nonnegative difference between congested and free-flow local shortest-path times is added to the reference 1,223-zone car skim. Journey components outside the local assignment network remain fixed.\n",
    "5. The five-alternative logit model recomputes Car, Walk, Bicycle, PT with walk access, and PT with bicycle access travel demand. Updated car travel demand is collapsed to gates and averaged with the same $1/k$ MSA step as link traffic volume.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is still a local-network approximation: travel times change on links in the local assignment network, including retained connecting links outside the cordon. Journey components beyond this network remain fixed. As the routes between different OD pairs traverse different internal zones and gates, the travel times between these OD pairs are thus updated based on zone- and gate-specific congested times."
   ]
  },
