   "source": [
    "**Reading the map.** Each horizontal line shows the infrastructure stage a plan keeps over the 40-year horizon, and the dot marks the stage chosen in Year 1. The *Baseline* stays in Stage 0 (no investment). *Static 1* builds Package 1, the Forch Central Mobility Hub Transformation (underground garage, new station square, bus terminal, e-buses and charging), and *Static 2* builds Package 1 and Package 2, the first-mile/last-mile active feeder network (cycleway network, bridges, bike facility, e-bike charging, Tempo 30 zones), together. The Package 2 row stays empty because no static plan builds it alone. It only appears as part of \"Both stages\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Committed vs. conditional decisions.** In Notebook 02, every decision is *committed*: the stage is chosen in Year 1, cannot be reversed, and does not depend on how demand, costs or the climate develop. There are no *conditional* decisions yet, which would be taken later if monitored conditions are met (for example, build Package 2 only if Package 1 reaches a target modal share). They will appear in the later notebooks as steps between rows, in the staged plans (schedule committed in advance) and in the flexible plan (investment triggered by observed conditions).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Plan | Committed in Year 1 | Conditional (decided later) |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Baseline | No investment | none |\n",
    "| Static 1 | Package 1 | none |\n",
    "| Static 2 | Packages 1 and 2 | none |"
   ]
  },
