   "source": [
    "Year-40 comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "In the do-nothing baseline (Stage 0), the distance-weighted modal split is 46.8 % car, 39.9 % PT, 9.4 % bicycle and 3.9 % walking. Average in-vehicle time is 13.56 min, road delay is 12.6 million person-hours per year, and operating CO2 is 148,344 t/year.\n",
    "\n",
    "Static 1: (Package 1, the Forch Central Mobility Hub Transformation, Stage 1) shifts the car share by −0.06 pp and the PT share by +0.05 pp. It reduces road delay by 21.0 thousand person-hours/year (−0.17 %) and operating CO2 by 174 t/year (−0.12 %). PT users gain only in transfer walking (−0.003 min per PT trip). Construction adds 5,000 t CO2, and the undiscounted 40-year infrastructure cost is CHF 0.043 billion.\n",
    "\n",
    "Static 2: (Packages 1 and 2, Stage 3) shifts the car share by −0.10 pp and the PT share by +0.10 pp, and reduces operating CO2 by 296 t/year (−0.20 %). Package 2 also lowers PT access (−0.004 min) and egress (−0.006 min) times per trip, which Package 1 does not. Road delay falls by 20.3 thousand person-hours/year, slightly less than in Static 1, and the in-vehicle time reduction is smaller (−0.0007 vs. −0.0020 min). Construction emissions are 7,200 t CO2 and the 40-year cost is CHF 0.070 billion.\n",
    "\n",
    "Interpretation: both plans move the system in the favourable direction for delay, in-vehicle time and operating CO2, at the price of higher construction emissions and cost. Package 2 adds about 122 t/year of further CO2 reduction for 2,200 t of construction CO2 and CHF 0.027 billion, but does not further reduce road delay. All effects are small relative to the baseline (below 0.3 % for every indicator), because the model covers all of Switzerland and the hub area is a small part of total demand. The modal-share changes are contextual, not welfare scores, and the \"annual trip equivalents\" are a mode-specific conversion of fixed peak demand, not additional trips. The section indicators (reference time, load/capacity, crowding) are n/a because no section is configured for this project.\n",
    "\n",
    "Consistency check: the three plans end in different stages (0, 1 and 3), so no two plans can be compared at the same stage. This end-state table does not show robustness under uncertainty. Timing of construction, accumulated benefits, lifecycle costs and discounted values can only be evaluated with the full deployment pathway in later notebooks."
   ]
  },
